 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "the r11 head registers every host input at the pin (p_* pin flops, 2-flop reset sync) and every output is a relay-fed pin register (o_io / o_ctl / status pad); a kit flop stage would add an unpriced edge (the r11 relays are priced in the RTL header: D=10, status 8)"
 },
 "structural_change": "r14: after r13_cl real NEEDS_RTL (TT -60.21ps / FF -102.73ps / DRC0). Registered 8-bit ordinal comparison partials and group status/fault bits break the agreement-tree-to-sticky-fault path; one existing final fault pad is consumed by the comparison stage, preserving every external fault/reset edge and D10/status8. Dedicated child clock leaf bins prevent child insertion targets skewing parent relays sharing a spatial bin. MAIN symmetric fanout8.",
